      "english": "All those who say, “We do not need to be taught,” or who do not submit in their hearts to those who teach, suffer from the disease of ignorance, which is the mother of pride. This pride was loved by those who, from the beginning, were prepared for destruction, those who were cast down from heaven, having been led astray by the pride of their own hearts, they did not subject themselves to those superior in virtue, but fled from their heavenly teachers.",
